# nr-office-ooxml-text-metrics: integration fragment

The module `text_metrics` of the crate mixdog-ooxml: `portable/text-metrics.mjs` (measureTextWidth, wrapParagraph with the
Korean kinsoku rules and the East Asian fallback family, measureTextBlock at 1.2 em per line, the per-face width
calibration, text-box fit, contrast, shape spacing, vertical balance, stat-label proximity, CJK tracking, the type-ladder
font-size repair). It measures through mixdog-fonts: the caller registers the faces in a `mixdog_fonts::registry::Registry`
(the provisioned Office faces included) and builds a `TextMeasurer`. No protocol method, service or SERVICE_PENDING name
belongs to it.

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/src/lib.rs

After `pub mod template_tokens;` (keep the list sorted) add:

    pub mod text_metrics;

and in the crate documentation, after "the document fingerprint ([`fingerprint`])" add "and the text metrics and layout
reviews ([`text_metrics`])".

## native/core/crates/mixdog-ooxml/Cargo.toml

[dependencies], after `mixdog-fsio = { workspace = true }`, add (the workspace entry comes from nr-office-fonts.wire):

    mixdog-fonts = { workspace = true }

(the module and tests/twin_text_metrics.rs also use mixdog-fsio, mixdog-js, sha2 and serde_json, which the crate already
lists). New dependency edge for Cargo.lock: mixdog-ooxml -> mixdog-fonts. Nothing else changes; mixdog-fonts must be a
workspace member and dependency first (nr-office-fonts.wire).

## native/core/fixtures/MANIFEST.json

In the "sets" list, after the entry of office-stats ... keep the list sorted by set name: "office-text-metrics" goes after
"office-stats" and before the next set; add:

    {
      "command": "node benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-text-metrics.mjs --tree <dir with node_modules>",
      "fileCount": 1,
      "manifest": "office-text-metrics/MANIFEST.json",
      "manifestSha256": "9ef3af42e2b7ee35ef0cd53f6d5ac35a95ec092d5a9efbc1d879fe84cad399ef",
      "recorder": "benchmarks/rust-core/recorders/record-office-text-metrics.mjs",
      "set": "office-text-metrics",
      "totalBytes": 378482
    }

(Recompute manifestSha256 and totalBytes from the committed office-text-metrics/MANIFEST.json and golden.json if the tool
that keeps this file reformats them.) The recording was made with `--tree C:/Project/mixdog` from a scratch checkout, so
product.commit in office-text-metrics/MANIFEST.json is null: re-run the recorder in the integration tree to fill it in.

## Not compiled

Written without cargo: the first `cargo test -p mixdog-ooxml` is the check. tests/twin_text_metrics.rs replays
native/core/fixtures/office-text-metrics (needs no Node; the Hangul cases need the provisioned Noto Sans KR installed with
the recorded sha256, as the office-measure twin does); twin_live_text_metrics (ignored) re-records through Node. The
measured widths are only as exact as mixdog-fonts' canvas measureText (its own twin, office-measure, reports how far that
is); a width that differs from the recording by more than 1e-3 there shows here first as a line-break difference.
